    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's a summary of the fixes I made:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n**1. Toxicity Metric Test Failure** (`src/eval/index.test.js`)\n- **Problem**: The `toxicityMetric` function expected `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but was being called by `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`. The references array was incorrectly passed as the banned terms, causing all safe outputs to be flagged as toxic.\n- **Fix**: Updated the function signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` so it matches the calling convention of other metrics while ignoring the references parameter.\n\n**2. Governance Module Export Failure** (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)\n- **Problem**: The test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it was only exported as part of the default export object.\n- **Fix**: Added explicit named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` from the governance module's `index.js` file.\n\nAll 28 tests across 8 test files now pass successfully, and all existing public exports are preserved.",
